From: Thomas Smith <thomsmit@google.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:01:06 -0500
Subject: [graphite] Gracefully handle pathological number of clip draws

* In the DrawListLayer system, clip draws are recorded immediately when updateForClipStack is called. However, these draws were not counted against the maximum draw pass draw limits, leading to scenarios where pipeline data structures could overflow.

* Now, needsFlushBeforeDraw ingests the clipElements, makes a second pass through the clip elements to count the undrawnElements, and uses this to count if drawListLayer is enabled.

* Additionally, if after flushing, the number of remaining clip draws exceeds the drawPass' max number of draws, the draw fails and logs a warning. This guards both sorting and layer systems.

Bug: b/574218401
Change-Id: Ie8a475b0936be6a958c26f701648ac0447dfd322
Reviewed-on: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1407316
Commit-Queue: Thomas Smith <thomsmit@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>
Auto-Submit: Thomas Smith <thomsmit@google.com>

